[[:db/retract 17592186072734 :answer-field/choices 17592186072736] [:db/retract 17592186072734 :answer-field/choices 17592186072737] [:db/retract 17592186072734 :answer-field/choices 17592186072738] [:db/retract 17592186072734 :answer-field/choices 17592186072739] [:db/retract 17592186072734 :answer-field/choices 17592186072735] {:db/id 17592186073795 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-91c5c1c2-4ce4-55a2-ac92-bbede8d9affd" "question-ba25bf3b-644a-5776-8a5e-2183fdce3e91" "question-311b03b5-e8f4-50ac-8092-f1ccfd08d0fe" "question-0d0d02e2-5948-5f96-a30c-cafd41b823b1" "question-5601730d-1a4d-5c97-8724-9bd6738cfc23"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073417 :question/worked-solution "In the model, we have $\\dfrac{\\color{red}1}{3}$ multiplied by ${\\color{blue}3}.$ This means that we need to make $\\color{blue}3$ copies of the given fraction model.\n\n![](images/38/38d0f24ab003913a30051d64dda233980173939825d9cc6f34473b1cbdcdbeed.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the missing fraction model is:\n\n![](images/ac/ac8618a503eb2cfd41a7fa8851cdb0dbb7152325100ec922b533d9da6e63b7c5.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073796 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9768bd40-ef16-5134-a90c-a2115761ab30" "question-2b86cc44-e53b-5bce-9e88-da200892d856" "question-89485e88-ee9b-5156-9fee-31a4b23231c2" "question-41a05529-6eba-5a2d-bed6-94e4b8737f7b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073418 :question/problem "![](images/5a/5aef67e5f151465f09eba64456f4566cc984c97857d8e6203cd25d60952e183a.png)\n\n \n\nUse the model above to calculate $3 \\times \\dfrac{1}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to multiply $\\dfrac{\\color{red}1}{5}$ by $\\color{blue}3$, we repeat the fraction model $\\color{blue}3$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](images/fe/fe41721739d82df825d2a7e28bc19590fbc784354a58aa74137aceda0e6be202.png)\n\n \n\nThere are ${\\color{blue}3} \\times {\\color{red}1} = 3$ shaded pieces in total. Therefore, \n\n$$\n3 \\times \\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac{3}{5}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073797 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4f0ca13e-f296-535a-b9b8-5e785e9a4856" "question-4122a212-e3ad-5dc5-8f5d-3acb14eb15ce" "question-e74bdd21-a2c2-52eb-8154-937a1aecf465" "question-2d3853ed-7ef3-5ab5-8f97-ff7d05e04575"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073419 :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{4}{9}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/ee/eef3cec4311b03e7f4be59e367cbd3d6947afd73b16a00b487f28ae7ea2bf8b8.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{9} \\times 4 = \\dfrac{4}{9}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** We can swap the factors on the left-hand side. So, the following would be a correct answer too:\n\n$$\n4 \\times \\dfrac{1}{9} = \\dfrac{4}{9}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073798 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0e935dd1-0b30-5386-b620-69533665772e" "question-1d25ca85-a4ba-5e9d-99c7-451877e700e3" "question-fc89f09e-3ad3-5777-acd5-6837ef9994f7" "question-43b90cb0-f452-5717-aab0-40519947c91d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073420 :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/c1/c1efa667a938907fcdd5ba9d0172b37a7efb0a7b312e3025556c4444814d2ab3.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $1$ shaded piece, and the shape on the right has $3$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of ${\\color{blue}3}.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{5} \\times {\\color{blue}3} = \\dfrac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is ${\\color{blue}3}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-91c5c1c2-4ce4-55a2-ac92-bbede8d9affd" :question/id #uuid "91c5c1c2-4ce4-55a2-ac92-bbede8d9affd" :question/math-academy-id "q-152015" :question/problem "![](images/19/19ffb261c2ccd3957c351e3e10afe3786f70a2c6d979c8eea8aa5b7fad80eb99.png)\n\nWhat picture is missing from the multiplication model above?" :question/worked-solution "In the model, we have $\\frac{1}{9}$ multiplied by $3.$ This means that we need to make $3$ copies of the given fraction model.\n\n![](images/61/611b6b31f7874808c9259a27380f061a670fff684dbc26cca7d27344ce4beba8.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](images/fe/fe0e8b40e5177040d28668325982dc5cb4065b62a3b4327290b78d457abbecb8.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d63736a2-0049-5da3-b9ea-dfee66076f49"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d63736a2-0049-5da3-b9ea-dfee66076f49" :answer-field/id #uuid "d63736a2-0049-5da3-b9ea-dfee66076f49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a044109c-9a91-5e0e-a36f-6a00890ba804" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06b0dd86-458a-5270-996b-bfb4e5cb9ac1" "answer-b086955e-affa-5ce4-8071-3a8753398d5a" "answer-f09df498-0f80-59b4-95c6-47993f6603d4" "answer-8b98febe-7738-546e-bcd0-7f5773855137" "answer-a044109c-9a91-5e0e-a36f-6a00890ba804"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06b0dd86-458a-5270-996b-bfb4e5cb9ac1" :answer/id #uuid "06b0dd86-458a-5270-996b-bfb4e5cb9ac1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/22/225d9811e413462b180aa41c32448e6c10c9bd069388882c2b1df337fb08c738.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b086955e-affa-5ce4-8071-3a8753398d5a" :answer/id #uuid "b086955e-affa-5ce4-8071-3a8753398d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/4d/4dac4a1ffda7fad12090dbbd3754d74634103ab901d36c452e6b7b83249ccb1f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f09df498-0f80-59b4-95c6-47993f6603d4" :answer/id #uuid "f09df498-0f80-59b4-95c6-47993f6603d4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/de/deef9cd5fcf21a19e8611b730495de93d53c4575a2a298c38b34d1beba29384a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b98febe-7738-546e-bcd0-7f5773855137" :answer/id #uuid "8b98febe-7738-546e-bcd0-7f5773855137" :answer/type :answer.type/image 