ed pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $3.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\times 3=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186072686 :answer-field/correct 17592186072689 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-0e935dd1-0b30-5386-b620-69533665772e" :question/id #uuid "0e935dd1-0b30-5386-b620-69533665772e" :question/math-academy-id "q-174181" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b1ee34f80acf0a7aafe7238497dff76b22e422d909d5429be06605c12c0ef15d.png)\n\nThe missing number from the multiplication problem above is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{1}{8}$ on the left and $\\frac{3}{8}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/ab/abab6ca3b021dd1a8d38ea55008707c374f03e52b930fa3fa6dd187fe7945047.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $1$ shaded piece, and the shape on the right has $3$ shaded pieces. So, the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $3.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{8}\\times 3=\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a1bc5bf2-fd23-5255-95ec-9f396018e320"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1bc5bf2-fd23-5255-95ec-9f396018e320" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1bc5bf2-fd23-5255-95ec-9f396018e320" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7b225564-3412-57e7-b8a6-dadaac97aa13" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7b225564-3412-57e7-b8a6-dadaac97aa13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b225564-3412-57e7-b8a6-dadaac97aa13" :answer/id #uuid "7b225564-3412-57e7-b8a6-dadaac97aa13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d25ca85-a4ba-5e9d-99c7-451877e700e3" :question/id #uuid "1d25ca85-a4ba-5e9d-99c7-451877e700e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-152072" :question/problem "![](images/b5/b5c08c943267b09fb9a1da2133c79bbf7a807f4f6865ba3824e3a28bd9035571.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the multiplication problem above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{1}{7}$ on the left and $\\frac{5}{7}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/16/16fba9ecbb17fc504413d656d8434c10b33f330e448ab9da24cd6105ad7251c6.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $1$ shaded piece, and the shape on the right has $5$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $5.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{7}\\times 5=\\frac{5}{7}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-87f8ee80-52f5-5a85-87d9-c211d09c2693"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-87f8ee80-52f5-5a85-87d9-c211d09c2693" :answer-field/id #uuid "87f8ee80-52f5-5a85-87d9-c211d09c2693" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cac10980-ed32-51b3-9d5d-c6514d5cad74" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cac10980-ed32-51b3-9d5d-c6514d5cad74" "answer-d5e2e566-b518-550e-9f3e-b59a1f9fa200" "answer-f9760b90-5969-5272-b63e-17258582d7ff" "answer-046d5ee1-bdcd-5df6-b759-1fcc3a6000c5" "answer-011d959c-931e-57ed-8699-e64bfa41c4f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cac10980-ed32-51b3-9d5d-c6514d5cad74" :answer/id #uuid "cac10980-ed32-51b3-9d5d-c6514d5cad74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5e2e566-b518-550e-9f3e-b59a1f9fa200" :answer/id #uuid "d5e2e566-b518-550e-9f3e-b59a1f9fa200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9760b90-5969-5272-b63e-17258582d7ff" :answer/id #uuid "f9760b90-5969-5272-b63e-17258582d7ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-046d5ee1-bdcd-5df6-b759-1fcc3a6000c5" :answer/id #uuid "046d5ee1-bdcd-5df6-b759-